WEBVTT

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:04.230
<b>Kushiro</b>

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:04.230
Sunfish?

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:08.980
The sunfish float to the surface 
of the water in summer to take a nap,

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:12.930
so you get on top of them and 
take out their meat and organs.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.870
You just want to eat some 
fish that's in season, don't you?

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.880
I sewed it back together.

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:28.050
Thank you.

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:30.380
You've done so much for me.

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.520
And Cikapasi, too.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:33.850
Not at all.

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:37.060
I feel so much safer on the 
road while a man's with me.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:42.440
You're cold to me, normally,

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.310
but when it counts, you're kind.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:50.420
You two married?

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.460
Want some meat?

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:57.360
He's offering us some sea otter meat.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:00.120
Sea otter? I've never had any.

00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:02.200
Thank you.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:05.310
Make sure the two of you eat it together.

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:08.250
What did he say?

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:15.450
I'll go get some beach rose fruit.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.330
What's that black cloud?

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:38.290
Oh, no... I hate grasshoppers.

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:41.160
And you call yourself "immortal."

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:43.170
This ain't good.

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:01.070
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.300
Aah!

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.850
They're biting at our clothes!

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:26.810
That police lodge!

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:29.520
Evacuate over there!

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:35.540
<b>Episode Twenty
 Blue Eyes</b>

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.680
Inkarmat should've been close...

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:34.040
It won't kill her!

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.210
Just get inside!

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:39.030
Ow!

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.700
What the hell is that?

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.160
A locust swarm.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:51.620
When you get the right conditions, after a 
flood or something, you get a ton of locusts.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:56.430
They move in swarms over 
dozens of kilometers.

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:58.020
They can cross the sea if they want to.

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:00.880
They'll eat your crops, of course,

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:03.980
but also the paper walls of 
your house and your kimono.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:08.170
How long does it take for them to pass by?

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:09.750
I'm hungry...

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:13.060
Is Asirpa-san okay?

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:19.610
Inkarmat!

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:22.610
Come here!

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:28.240
You saved me.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:29.870
It's safe out here.

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:33.090
I wanted to talk to you alone.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:34.580
This is a good chance.

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:38.200
Tell me everything you know about my father.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:48.800
Sea otter meat has a... unique... scent.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:51.510
Can we really eat this?

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:56.980
<i>Something's wrong...</i>

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:01.230
<i>Shiraishi just looked... sexy.</i>

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:03.910
Sugimoto, you okay?

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:11.590
Oh, dear. My button burst off again.

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:15.460
<i>That Matagi... is so hot!</i>

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:20.750
I feel so dizzy...

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.210
Are you okay, Ogata?

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:24.070
Lie down! Now!

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:28.600
Let's unbutton your shirt 
so you can breathe better.

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:31.300
Take off his pants, too. No, everything!

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:37.670
Ow! They bit my ears!

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:42.650
Hey there, guys.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:44.410
Kiroranke...

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:50.330
I knew your father well.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:54.020
I met him when I was your age.

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:56.830
Do you hate him?

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:58.730
Of course not.

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:01.800
I've always been on his side, and yours.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:03.810
Do you think I'll believe that?

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:09.510
You used lies to scare Huci, 
and used Tanigaki to follow me.

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:12.260
I didn't lie to Huci.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:14.770
You should return to Otaru.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:16.880
I don't believe in fortune-telling.

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:20.560
I'm going to find out the truth myself.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:26.570
Nopperabo, the man in Abashiri Prison,
 isn't your father.

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:35.660
Your father, Wilk, wasn't the kind of man 
who could kill Ainu and steal their gold.

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:40.840
When I first met him,
 Wilk had just come to Hokkaido,

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:43.530
and spoke Ainu with a Sakhalin accent.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:46.970
He had deep blue eyes, like yours.

00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:53.300
He said he was born of a Polish father
 and a Sakhalin Ainu mother.

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:57.320
He said that Sakhalin was filled with Poles

00:06:56.030 --> 00:07:01.310
<b>Sakhalin</b>

00:06:57.320 --> 00:07:01.310
who had been oppressed by the 
czar and exiled to the Far East.

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:05.020
Ever since he was young, Wilk had worked 
with the other ethnic minorities

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:08.440
to try and obtain liberation from the czar.

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:10.200
He fought, was wounded,

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:13.800
and fled to Otaru in Hokkaido.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:19.680
At the time, I'd already begun my 
career as a wandering fortune-teller.

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:22.290
I spent every day with him.

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:27.760
Wilk accepted what I told him of the Ainu.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:32.210
Our beliefs, customs, language, 
food... everything.

00:07:33.170 --> 00:07:40.490
He recovered from his wounds here, 
and came to love the Hokkaido Ainu.

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:48.150
I don't believe my father
 is Nopperabo, either.

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:52.530
But my father never told me about you!

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:56.830
My father said he learned 
everything from my mother.

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:59.380
I don't believe anything you say!

00:08:04.070 --> 00:08:07.400
To Wilk, I was still a child.

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:11.340
Maybe he forgot me.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:16.260
If you say Nopperabo is a different person,

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:18.050
then where is my father now?

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:22.270
He's gone.

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:26.020
Wilk was murdered.

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:30.820
By Kiroranke, his former friend.

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:41.500
I got separated from Hijikata's group 
at Asahikawa, and haven't seen them since.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:47.960
I guessed that you'd head down the 
mountains to Tokachi to avoid the 7th.

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:52.380
And then I heard at a local 
kotan that someone saw you.

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:54.840
Anyway...

00:08:54.840 --> 00:09:01.810
Sugimoto, you've gotten a lot...
 hotter... since we last met.

00:09:02.710 --> 00:09:04.350
Stop it.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:05.400
<i>So cute.</i>

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:06.550
<i>So cute.</i>

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:07.440
<i>So cute!</i>

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:12.470
Kiro-chan, you look like 
you've been working out, too.

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:14.220
You think so?

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:15.850
What do you think, Tanigaki?

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:20.160
<i>What is this feeling...?</i>

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:21.740
<i>I can't control it!</i>

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:25.250
<i>I've never felt this before!</i>

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:28.040
<i>How do I get rid of this feeling?</i>

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:38.760
But... I can't... control it anymore!

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:42.720
Let's play sumo!

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:45.110
<i>Wow, great idea!</i>

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:10.750
Good times.

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:18.970
The grasshoppers are gone.

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:21.820
Yeah...

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:24.930
We got a little out of control.

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:26.820
Yeah...

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:29.830
Tell no one of this.

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:30.900
Yeah.

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:45.610
Inkarmat...

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:51.430
It's believed that the meat of the sea otters
 functions as a powerful aphrodisiac.

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:57.830
When one of them loses a partner, they have 
no outlet for their lusts, and they die.

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:02.120
W-Wait!

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:03.390
What's gotten into you?

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:08.850
You can blame it on the sea otter
 meat you ate, Tanigaki Nispa.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:25.910
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:35.650
<i>If you go to Abashiri,
you'll run into Kiroranke again.</i>

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:38.380
He's a very dangerous man.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:42.570
You'll lose both the gold 
and the tattoos in the end.

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:46.850
I can't imagine that Kiroranke Nispa
 would kill my father.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:49.560
I have proof.

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:52.850
Asirpa-chan!

00:11:54.850 --> 00:11:56.610
You were there all night?

00:11:56.610 --> 00:12:00.210
Oh, there you are. It's Asirpa-chan!

00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:02.770
I'm so glad you're safe.

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:06.740
<i>Kiroranke!</i>

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:08.550
<i>What are you doing here?</i>

00:12:10.010 --> 00:12:12.040
Hey, Asirpa.

00:12:15.970 --> 00:12:20.010
Kiroranke Nispa, did you kill my father?

00:12:21.990 --> 00:12:23.220
Me?

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:25.760
Where's this coming from?

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:31.350
<i>She confronted him directly 
right after I told her. Silly girl.</i>

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:33.100
The proof is...

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:36.020
...the fingerprints left
on this betting ticket.

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:37.530
What?

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:38.730
Fingerprints?

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:40.600
Inkarmat!

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:44.200
Every set of fingerprints is different.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:49.320
Outside of Japan, they've been using them in 
criminal investigations for several years.

00:12:50.630 --> 00:12:55.410
At the horse racing track in Naganuma, 
I took fingerprints from the men,

00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:57.170
and had them matched.

00:12:57.170 --> 00:13:01.510
<b>Hokkaido Horse Racing Association
Betting Ticket</b>

00:12:57.560 --> 00:13:03.720
Kiroranke-san's matched those taken 
several years ago at a certain place...

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:07.970
The place where Asirpa-chan's 
father was murdered.

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:10.220
Murdered?

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:14.640
There were fingerprints on 
his makiri blade, she says.

00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:18.020
You said you hadn't seen 
my father for years, right?

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:19.550
Come on.

00:13:19.550 --> 00:13:20.910
If I'm the killer,

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:23.400
then who's Nopperabo, the guy in the prison?

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:24.780
Hold it.

00:13:25.210 --> 00:13:28.990
She's working with Lt. Tsurumi.

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:31.450
Stop! What proof do you have?

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:34.430
Tanigaki Genjirou...

00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:36.710
She seduced you over to her side, huh?

00:13:37.190 --> 00:13:41.460
It was Lt. Tsurumi who recovered 
the items left at the murder scene.

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:45.970
In other words, he's the only one 
with the recorded fingerprints.

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:52.150
I was just using Lt. Tsurumi.

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:56.440
One hell of a woman, ain't she, Tanigaki?

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:00.150
You believe information 
given to you by Lt. Tsurumi?

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:03.690
If we start killing each other, 
that's just what he wants.

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:05.300
Right?

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:07.380
Asirpa...

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:12.030
I understand that you don't want 
to believe your father is Nopperabo.

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:16.250
But there can't be that many people in 
the world capable of coming up with the idea

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:19.170
of tattooing a code on human skins.

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:22.630
You know that, don't you?

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:26.370
Which of them is it?

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:28.720
Which one is telling the truth?

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:33.700
Shiraishi...

00:14:34.130 --> 00:14:38.440
You're the only one here 
who met Nopperabo in jail.

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:42.500
Did he really have blue eyes like Asirpa-san?

00:14:43.350 --> 00:14:47.580
I never said he had blue eyes.

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:51.810
I always tried to avoid 
staring at his nasty face.

00:14:52.310 --> 00:14:55.080
Does Nopperabo really have no face?

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:59.120
All he ever did was 
silently make the tattoos.

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:05.610
The escape plan itself came down to 
the prisoners from Hijikata Toshizou.

00:15:08.710 --> 00:15:13.570
Maybe Hijikata Toshizou 
set the whole thing up?

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:20.890
I don't know what you want, Inkarmat.

00:15:21.250 --> 00:15:25.650
I want to protect the gold, 
as an Ainu woman.

00:15:26.260 --> 00:15:30.910
Did Asirpa's father, Wilk, feel the same way?

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:32.050
Yes.

00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:36.260
That's why he was killed by Kiroranke,
a fellow member of his guerrilla organization.

00:15:37.030 --> 00:15:39.080
That's what I think.

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:43.420
It's possible that the fingerprints 
were falsified by Lt. Tsurumi.

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:45.770
I can't prove that you're wrong.

00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:49.930
But if I end up dead in the future,

00:15:50.900 --> 00:15:53.560
it will be Kiroranke who kills me.

00:15:54.650 --> 00:15:59.020
Did you sleep with me to 
protect yourself from him?

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:01.910
No.

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:05.350
What happened last night was 
due to the sea otter stew.

00:16:05.350 --> 00:16:06.450
<i>Sea otter!</i>

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:13.010
<b>Otaru</b>

00:16:09.170 --> 00:16:14.200
Another telegram came to the old Ainu 
lady in Otaru from Tanigaki in Kushiro.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.700
He's met up with them, it seems.

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:18.280
Good.

00:16:19.010 --> 00:16:22.870
I think it's time for us to 
head to Abashiri too, then.

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:27.090
My sons are Hokkaido Ainu.

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:30.550
The gold exists for the Ainu of this land.

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:33.810
My goal is the same as yours.

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:37.010
So, what do we do?

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:39.470
Everybody is suspicious of each other.

00:16:39.780 --> 00:16:42.930
I don't want anybody killing me in my sleep.

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:51.820
We have to go.

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:56.900
When we meet Nopperabo,
 we'll know if he's Asirpa's father.

00:16:57.540 --> 00:17:01.490
Our goal of going to Abashiri hasn't changed.

00:17:02.280 --> 00:17:03.580
So let's do this.

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:05.830
Inkarmat, Kiroranke...

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:09.300
If one of you ends up dead on our journey...

00:17:10.070 --> 00:17:13.860
I'll automatically kill the other one.

00:17:15.210 --> 00:17:16.220
Just kidding.

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:33.190
New kid.

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:37.790
You curious about that guy?

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:39.280
Yeah, I guess.

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:43.540
You don't see many people 
with faces like that.

00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:48.370
Let me give you a warning, 
since I've been here longer.

00:17:48.820 --> 00:17:54.290
The first thing you have to learn 
here is to stay away from Nopperabo.

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:23.910
Nopperabo is transferred from one cell
 to another almost every day.

00:18:24.270 --> 00:18:27.580
If there's any kind of pattern 
to the way they're moving him,

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:30.210
we may be able to predict 
where he'll be in a few days.

00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:40.760
So this is a pig farm?

00:18:41.210 --> 00:18:43.680
There are crates back there.

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:45.650
Carry them outside.

00:18:45.650 --> 00:18:47.160
Okay.

00:18:50.130 --> 00:18:51.140
New kid...

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:54.170
Leave your katana.

00:18:54.170 --> 00:18:57.510
If you trip on it,
you'll end up covered in pig shit.

00:18:57.510 --> 00:18:58.700
Okay...

00:19:02.020 --> 00:19:04.410
Where are the crates?

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:06.100
Chief Kadokura?

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:12.840
So that new kid is working with the 7th?

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:16.800
Take care of him, Security Chief Kadokura.

00:19:17.270 --> 00:19:19.260
You want me to do it?

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:21.840
Use the prisoners.

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:24.730
They're all good at murder.

00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:27.970
This is my prison.

00:19:28.820 --> 00:19:33.330
Anybody who tries to mess 
with me will end up as pig food.

00:19:35.210 --> 00:19:38.110
<i>Don't hate me for this, new kid.</i>

00:19:44.600 --> 00:19:47.450
Ch-Chief Kadokura...?

00:19:51.640 --> 00:19:53.310
Chief Kadokura!

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:54.790
Where are you?

00:19:55.430 --> 00:19:57.350
Huh? My katana...

00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:17.770
Chief Kadokura...

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:20.330
<i>You've gotta be kidding me!</i>

00:20:20.330 --> 00:20:22.360
<i>He's really strong!</i>

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:26.210
<i>I don't pick fights I can't win.</i>

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:31.250
I fed him to the pigs. Just like you said.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:33.960
He fought harder than expected,

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:37.370
and both the new kid and the 
prisoners were badly wounded.

00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:40.210
I finished all three of them.

00:20:41.110 --> 00:20:46.820
I reported the new kid as missing and 
the other two as dying after a brawl.

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:52.070
Chief Kadokura, you've been 
here seven years, right?

00:20:52.070 --> 00:20:52.730
Yeah.

00:20:53.300 --> 00:20:58.470
I always thought of you as a wimpy tanuki 
of a man, with limp, flaccid balls.

00:20:59.080 --> 00:21:02.740
I assumed that if I looked up "useless" 
in the dictionary, I'd see your picture.

00:21:03.440 --> 00:21:09.200
But today, I'm going to adjust 
my opinion of you just a little.

00:21:10.090 --> 00:21:11.530
Thanks...

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:14.210
I'll never forget that.

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:19.710
I had more research to do here.

00:21:20.330 --> 00:21:22.710
I underestimated Chief Kadokura.

00:21:24.100 --> 00:21:26.930
Lt. Tsurumi will scold me!

00:23:08.210 --> 00:23:09.070
What?

00:23:13.380 --> 00:23:15.340
Damn it! I can't see a thing!

00:23:15.340 --> 00:23:16.180
Where are they?

00:23:19.140 --> 00:23:21.370
Leave the horses and the money.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Next Time:
The Sound of an Ambush</b>

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:39.380
Next Time: "The Sound of an Ambush."
